  "content": [
    {
      "text": "A Hebrew designation meaning “the most high God,” as in Gen. 14:18–20, 22. It is the name for deity worshipped by Melchizedek, king of Salem, and appears for the first time in the Bible in Gen. 14:18. It is found also in Acts 16:17; see also D&C 59:10–12; 76:112.",
